2025-12-23 00:18:18 | INFO | Q234 id=Ou2vtire_Js_00-00-00_00-00-16 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The audio segment between 3 and 4 seconds features a distinct upward pitch shift on a guitar string followed by a return to the original pitch.\n\n1.  **Analyze the sound:** The sound produced is a note that is raised in pitch significantly and then immediately drops back down.\n2.  **Evaluate the choices against the sound:**\n    *   **A) Hammer-on:** This involves striking a string to sound a note and then fretting a higher note on the same string without picking again. This results in a smooth transition to a higher note, not a pitch bend and release.\n    *   **B) Pull-off:** This involves plucking a note and then pulling the finger off to sound a lower note already fretted on the same string. This results in a smooth transition to a lower note, not a pitch bend and release.\n    *   **C) Bend release:** This technique involves bending the string up (or down) to raise (or lower) the pitch, and then releasing the tension to return the pitch to its original, unbent state. The sound heard perfectly matches this description: a pitch is raised and then released.\n    *   **D) Slide:** This involves moving a finger along a fretted string to transition between two notes, resulting in a continuous sweep of pitch, not a distinct bend and return.\n\nThe sound clearly demonstrates a pitch being raised and then returned to its original level, which is characteristic of a bend release.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
2025-12-23 00:18:20 | INFO | Q235 id=GJ6r_T6ckc4_00-00-00_00-00-06 | baseline_pred=A | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=A | followup_correct=False | raw=The audio provided consists of a sequence of short and long beeps, which is characteristic of Morse code.\n\nThe sequence of beeps is:\nShort-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot) - Long-Long-Long (dash-dash-dash) - Short-Short-Short (dot-dot-dot)\n\nIn the International Morse Code:\n*   Three short signals ($\cdot\cdot\cdot$) represent the letter 'S'.\n*   Three long signals (---) represent the letter 'O'.\n\nTherefore, the sequence $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ --- $\cdot\cdot\cdot$ decodes to "SOS".\n\nComparing this to the choices:\nA) sOS\nB) cODE\nC) hELLO\nD) wORLD\n\nThe decoded message matches choice A.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
