tions strongly suggests a state of **nervousness** or anxiety about the situation indicated by the sounds.\n\nThe sequence of a notification sound followed by a heavy sigh strongly suggests a reaction to something stressful or anticipated, fitting the description of nervousness better than simple impatience.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{A}$
