oured out, it suggests he would have preferred it to be consumed or saved, which aligns with being protective or stingy with the drink.\n\nIf the second man was stingy, he wouldn't want the drink poured out as a tribute; he would want it drunk. His comment directly criticizes the act of pouring it out as a waste.\n\nTherefore, the most plausible inference for why he would call pouring a drink out a "waste" is that he is protective of the drink, suggesting he is stingy with it and didn't want it poured out.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{D}$
