2025-12-23 00:43:05 | INFO | Q676 id=BV11yrkYME4G_00-03-24_00-03-43 | baseline_pred=C | gold=C | prompt_variant=strong | followup_pred=C | followup_correct=True | raw=The user is asking to identify which of the three acids mentioned in the audio (sulfuric acid, hydrochloric acid, or nitric acid) has the strongest acidity, based on their $\text{pK}_a$ values provided in the audio.\n\n1.  **Identify the acids and their $\text{pK}_a$ values from the audio:**\n    *   Sulfuric acid ($\text{H}_2\text{SO}_4$): $\text{pK}_a = -1.3$ (The audio says "硫酸的 $\text{pK}$ 是 $-1.3$").\n    *   Hydrochloric acid ($\text{HCl}$): $\text{pK}_a = -7$ (The audio says "盐酸是 $-7$").\n    *   Nitric acid ($\text{HNO}_3$): $\text{pK}_a = -3$ (The audio says "硝酸是 $-3$").\n    *   *Note: The audio mentions "硫酸" (sulfuric acid) with $\text{pK}_a = -1.3$, "硝酸" (nitric acid) with $\text{pK}_a = -3$, and "盐酸" (hydrochloric acid) with $\text{pK}_a = -7$. The audio actually says "硫酸的 $\text{pK}$ 是 $-1.3$", "硝酸是 $-3$", and "盐酸是 $-7$". Let's re-listen carefully to the order mentioned in the audio: "硝酸的 $\text{pK}$ 是 $-1.3$", "硫酸是 $-3$", "而盐酸是 $-7$".*\n\n    Let's re-verify the mapping based on the audio sequence:\n    *   First acid mentioned: 硝酸 (Nitric acid) $\rightarrow \text{pK}_a = -1.3$\n    *   Second acid mentioned: 硫酸 (Sulfuric acid) $\rightarrow \text{pK}_a = -3$\n    *   Third acid mentioned: 盐酸 (Hydrochloric acid) $\rightarrow \text{pK}_a = -7$\n\n2.  **Determine the strongest acid:** Acidity is inversely related to the $\text{pK}_a$ value. The lower (more negative) the $\text{pK}_a$, the stronger the acid.\n\n    Comparing the values:\n    *   Nitric acid: $-1.3$\n    *   Sulfuric acid: $-3$\n    *   Hydrochloric acid: $-7$\n\n    The lowest value is $-7$, which corresponds to Hydrochloric acid (盐酸).\n\n3.  **Match with choices:**\n    A) sulfurous acid (Not mentioned with a value)\n    B) sulfuric acid ($\text{pK}_a = -3$)\n    C) hydrochloric acid ($\text{pK}_a = -7$)\n    D) nitric acid ($\text{pK}_a = -1.3$)\n\nHydrochloric acid has the lowest $\text{pK}_a$ value ($-7$) and is therefore the strongest acid among the three listed in the audio.\n\nThe correct choice is C.\n\nAnswer: $\boxed{C}$
