e rejects physical intimacy in favor of money ("I don't want your body, I want my money"). This strongly suggests a prioritization of work/studies over romance.\n    *   **C) he has lost faith in love:** While he mentions his "past," the primary theme is prioritizing work/money over immediate romantic/sexual opportunities, not necessarily a loss of faith in the concept of love itself.\n    *   **D) the girls who pursue him are all busier than him:** The evidence shows girls *are* pursuing him (offering drinks, taking off clothes), but he is the one rejecting the advances based on his priorities (math/money).\n\n3.  **Conclusion:** The strongest inference supported by the lyrics ("I will rather do my math" and rejecting physical advances for money) is that he prioritizes his work/studies over pursuing or engaging with interested girls.\n\nThe best fit is B.\n\nAnswer: \boxed{B}
